&Q000416 = A praise poem of Šulgi (Šulgi X)
@composite
#project: etcslatf/inter
#atf: use unicode
#atf: use math
#etcsl: text-id=c.2.4.2.24
#key: after http://etcsl.orinst.ox.ac.uk/cgi-bin/etcsl.cgi?text=c.2.4.2.24&display=Crit&charenc=gcirc#

1. lugal# ma₂ na-mu-u₅
#tr.en: The king sailed to @wSN{Unug} towards the princely divine powers.
#lem: lugal[king]; ma[ship]; u[ride]
#etcsl: line-id=1

2. [ki unug]{[ki]}-ge# me nam-nun-na-še₃
#tr.en: @wGN{Sumer} and @wGN{Akkad} marvelled at him as he
#lem: ki[place]; Unug[1]SN; me[Being]; namnun[magnificence]
#etcsl: line-id=2

3. [ki-en]-gi ki-uri u₆ mu-e
#tr.en: moored the boat at the quay of @wSN{Kulaba}.
#lem: Kengir[1]; Akkad[1 Akkad]; u[admiration]; e[speak]
#etcsl: line-id=3

4. kar! kul-ab₄{ki}-ba-ke₄ ma₂ na-ga-am₃-mi-in-us₂
#tr.en: With a large wild bull of the mountains with uplifted horns,
#lem: kar[harbor]; Kulaba[1]SN; ma[ship]; us[accompany]
#etcsl: line-id=4

5. am gal hur-saŋ-ŋa₂ a₂ il₂-il₂-la-da
#tr.en: and with a sheep led by the hand
#lem: am[wild bull]; gal[big]; hursaŋ[mountain]; a[arm]; il[raise]
#etcsl: line-id=5

6. udu en zid-de₃ šu-a la₂-a-da
#tr.en: of an @fsux{en} priest at his right side,
#lem: udu[sheep]; en[priest]; zid[right]; šu[hand]; la[hang]
#etcsl: line-id=6

7. maš₂ su₄ maš₂ za la₂ gaba-a tab-ba-da
#tr.en: with a dappled kid and a bearded kid clasped to his breast,
#lem: maš[goat]; su[red]; maš[goat]; sum[beard]; la[hang]; gaba[breast]; tab[double]
#etcsl: line-id=7

8. {d}inana-ra eš₃ e₂-an-na-ka mu-na-da-an-ku₄-ku₄-u₃
#tr.en: he entered before @wDN{Inana} in the shrine of @wTN{E-ana}.
#lem: Inanak[1]DN; eš[shrine]; Eanak[1]TN; kur[enter]
#etcsl: line-id=8

9. sipad zid šul-gi-re šag₄ ki aŋ₂ tug₂-ba₁₃ tug₂ mu-mur₁₀
#tr.en: @wRN{Šulgi}, the good shepherd,
#lem: sipad[shepherd]; zid[right]; Šulgir[1]RN; šag[heart]; ki[place]; aŋ[measure]; ba[garment]; tug[textile]; mur[dress]
#etcsl: line-id=9

10. hi-li men-še₃ saŋ-ŋa₂ mi-ni-ŋal₂
#tr.en: a heart in love,
#lem: hili[attractiveness]; men[tiara]; saŋ[head]; ŋal[⟦be⟧ to be (there]
#etcsl: line-id=10

11. {d}inana-ke₄ u₆ mu-ni-dug₄
#tr.en: dressed himself in the @fsux{ba} garment and put a @fsux{ḫili} wig on his head as a crown.
#lem: Inanak[1]DN; u[admiration]; dug[speak]
#etcsl: line-id=11

12. ni₂-te-ni-še₃ šir₃ ba-ši-ni-ra
#tr.en: @wDN{Inana} looked at him with admiration and spontaneously struck up a song,
#lem: ni[self]; šir[sing]; rah[beat]
#etcsl: line-id=12

13. en₃-du-še₃! im-e
#tr.en: singing the words:
#lem: endu[song]; e[speak]
#etcsl: line-id=13

14. lugal-ra %e u₃-mu-un-ra
#tr.en: @q[Inana,Culgi]{“When I have bathed for the king,
#lem: lugal[king]; umun[lord]N
#etcsl: line-id=14

15. a mu-na-tu₁₇-a-gin₇
#tr.en: for the lord,
#lem: a[water]; tu[cvve]
#etcsl: line-id=15

16. %e su-ba %e du₅-mu-zid-ra %s a mu-na-tu₁₇-a-gin₇
#tr.en: when I have bathed for the shepherd @wDN{Dumuzid},
#lem: subad[shepherd]N; Dumuzid[1]DN; a[water]; tu[cvve]
#etcsl: line-id=16

17. im da-ŋu₁₀ šu tag-ge₄ dug₄-ga-gin₇
#tr.en: when I have adorned my flanks (?) with ointment (?),
#lem: im[clay]; dag[side]; šu[hand]; tag[touch]; dug[speak]
#etcsl: line-id=17

18. %e u₃ %s šembulugₓ(|ŠIM×UH₃|)-ga ka-ŋu₁₀ gun₅-gun₅-na-gin₇
#tr.en: when I have anointed my mouth with balsamic oil (?),
#lem: u[oil]N; bulug[a resin]; kag[mouth]; gunu[speckled]
#etcsl: line-id=18

19. šembi₂-zid %e i₃-bi₂-ŋa₂ mi-ni-mar-mar-ra-gin₇
#tr.en: when I have painted my eyes with kohl,
#lem: šembizida[kohl]; ibi[eye]; mar[place]V/t
#etcsl: line-id=19

20. šu %e na-aŋ₂-sag₉-ga-na-ka
#tr.en: when he has
#lem: šu[hand]; naŋsag[pleasure]
#etcsl: line-id=20

21. ib₂-ib₂-ŋu₁₀ mi-ni-dim₂-dim₂-ma₃-gin₇
#tr.en: …… my hips with his fair hands,
#lem: ib[hips]; dim[create]
#etcsl: line-id=21

22. %e u₃-mu-un %s i₃-nu₂ kug {d}inana{na}-še₃
#tr.en: when the lord who lies down beside holy @wDN{Inana},
#lem: umun[lord]N; nud[lie down]; kug[purify]; Inanak[1]DN
#etcsl: line-id=22

23. %e su-ba %e du₅-mu-zid-de₃
#tr.en: the shepherd @wDN{Dumuzid},
#lem: subad[shepherd]N; Dumuzid[1]DN
#etcsl: line-id=23

24. ur₂-ra ga i₃-du₈-a-na-gin₇
#tr.en: has …… on his lap,
#lem: ur[root]; ga[milk]; du[spread]
#etcsl: line-id=24

25. X IM a₂ gi-rin-ŋa₂ GI₄ in-tenₓ(GUR₈)-tenₓ(GUR₈)-na-gin₇
#tr.en: when he has relaxed (?) …… in my pure (?) arms,
#lem: X; X; a[arm]; girim[flower]; X; ten[extinguish]
#etcsl: line-id=25

26. [...] X saŋ kaš! saŋ-gin₇
#tr.en: when he has intercourse (?) with me …… like choice beer,
#lem: X; X; saŋ[head]; kaš[beer]; saŋ[head]
#etcsl: line-id=26

27. %e mu-uš %s mu-tag-ga-gin₇
#tr.en: when he ruffles my pubic hair for me,
#lem: meš[penis]N; tag[touch]
#etcsl: line-id=27

28. siki-ur₂-ŋu₁₀ ŋa₂-an-suh₃#-[suh₃-a-gin₇]
#tr.en: when he plays with the hair of my head,
#lem: sikiʾur[pubic hair]; suh[confuse]
#etcsl: line-id=28

29. siki-pa-ŋu₁₀ a-ne in-da-an-dug₄-ga-gin₇
#tr.en: when he lays his hands on my holy genitals,
#lem: sikipa[head hair]; ene[pleasure?]; dug[speak]
#etcsl: line-id=29

30. gal₄ kug-ŋa₂ šu %e bi₂-in-ma-ra-gin₇
#tr.en: when he lies down in the
#lem: gala[female genitals]; kug[pure]; šu[hand]; mar[place]V/t
#etcsl: line-id=30

31. šag₄ %e ze₂-ba-ŋa₂ %s u₃ [...] X-bi i₃-X-nu₂#-a-gin₇
#tr.en: …… of my sweet womb,
#lem: šag[heart]; zeb[good]V/i; u[sleep]; X; X; nud[lie down]
#etcsl: line-id=31

32. ma₂ MI-ni-gin₇ mu-X-[...]-AN#-gin₇
#lem: ma[ship]; X; X
#etcsl: line-id=32

33. ma₂ sal-la-ni-gin₇ mu-un-til-til-la-gin₇
#lem: ma[ship]; sal[thin]; til[complete]
#etcsl: line-id=33

34. ki-nu₂-a mi₂ ŋa₂-ni-dug₄-ga-a-gin₇
#tr.en: when he treats me tenderly on the bed,
#lem: kinud[sleeping quarter]; mi[cvne]; dug[speak]
#etcsl: line-id=34

35. %e u₃-mu-un-ra %s mi₂  %e  da-an-dug₄  %s 
#tr.en: then I will too treat my lord tenderly.”}
#lem: umun[lord]N; mi[cvne]; dug[speak]
#etcsl: line-id=35

36. %e na-aŋ₂ ze₂-eb₂ %s du₁₀-mu-ni-ib₂-tar{ar}
#tr.en: @q{“I will decree a good fate for him!
#lem: naŋ[fate]N; zeb[good]V/i; tar[cut]
#etcsl: line-id=36

37. sipad zid šul-gi-ra mi₂  %e  da-an-dug₄  %s 
#tr.en: I will treat @wRN{Šulgi},
#lem: sipad[shepherd]; zid[right]; Šulgir[1]RN; mi[cvne]; dug[speak]
#etcsl: line-id=37

38. %e na-aŋ₂ ze₂-eb₂ %s du₁₀-mu-ni-ib₂-tar{ar}
#tr.en: the good shepherd, tenderly!
#lem: naŋ[fate]N; zeb[good]V/i; tar[cut]
#etcsl: line-id=38

39. a₂-gar₃-ra-na mi₂-eš₂  %e  da-an-dug₄  %s 
#tr.en: I will decree a good fate for him!
#lem: X; mi[cvne]; dug[speak]
#etcsl: line-id=39

40. %e na-aŋ₂-sipad %s kur-kur-ra
#tr.en: I will treat him tenderly in his ……!
#lem: naŋsipad[shepherdship]; kur[mountain(s)]
#etcsl: line-id=40

41. %e na-aŋ₂-še₃ %s du₁₀-mu-ni-ib₂-tar{ar}
#tr.en: I will decree the shepherdship of all the lands as his destiny!”}
#lem: naŋ[fate]N; tar[cut]
#etcsl: line-id=41

42. nin su₃-ra₂-aŋ₂ an-na
#tr.en: The lady, the light of heaven, the delight of the black-headed, the youthful woman who excels her mother, who was granted divine powers by her father, @wDN{Inana}, the daughter of @wDN{Suen}, decreed a destiny for @wDN{Šulgi}, the son of @wDN{Ninsumun}:
#lem: nin[lady]; sudaŋ[precious metal or material (possibly amber)]; an[sky]
#etcsl: line-id=42

43. hi-li saŋ gig₂-ga
#lem: hili[attractiveness]; saŋ[head]; giggig[black]
#etcsl: line-id=43

44. munus šul-la ama-ni-ra dirig-ga
#lem: munus[woman]; šul[youth]; ama[mother]; dirig[make more than]
#etcsl: line-id=44

45. a-a-ni me ba-a
#lem: aya[father]; me[Being]; ba[allot]
#etcsl: line-id=45

46. {d}inana dumu {d}suen-na-ke₄
#lem: Inanak[1]DN; dumu[child]; Suen[1]DN
#etcsl: line-id=46

47. šul-gi dumu {d}nin-sumun₂-ka-ra
#lem: Šulgir[1]RN; dumu[child]; Ninsumunak[1]DN
#etcsl: line-id=47

48. nam mu-ni-ib₂-tar-re
#lem: nam[fate]; tar[cut]
#etcsl: line-id=48

49. me₃-a igi-še₃ ŋen-zu ŋe₂₆-me-en₃
#tr.en: @q[Inana,Culgi]{“In battle I will be the one who goes before you.
#lem: me[battle]; igi[eye]; ŋen[go]; ŋaʾe[I]
#etcsl: line-id=49

50. šen-šen-na kuš₇-gin₇ tukul la₂-zu-me-en₃
#tr.en: In combat I will carry your weapon like a personal attendant.
#lem: šen[battle]; kuš[high official]; tukul[weapon]; la[hang]
#etcsl: line-id=50

51. unken-na ka-mud-ŋal₂-zu-me-en₃
#tr.en: In the assembly I will be your advocate.
#lem: unkin[assembly]; kamudŋal[advocate]
#etcsl: line-id=51

52. har-ra-an-na zi-šag₄-ŋal₂-zu ŋe₂₆-me-en
#tr.en: On campaign I will be your encouragement.
#lem: harran[route]; zišagŋal[encouragement]; ŋaʾe[I]
#etcsl: line-id=52

53. sipad šag₄-ge pad₃-da X kug-ga-me-en₃
#tr.en: You are the shepherd chosen by holy …….
#lem: sipad[shepherd]; šag[heart]; pad[find]; X; kug[pure]
#etcsl: line-id=53

54. lugal u₂-a zid e₂-an-na-me-en₃
#tr.en: You are the king and generous provider of @wTN{E-ana}.
#lem: lugal[king]; ua[provisioner]; zid[right]; Eanak[1]TN
#etcsl: line-id=54

55. šuba₃ iri₁₂-gal an-na-me-en₃
#tr.en: You are the pure (?) one of @wDN{An's}@wTN{Iri-gal}.
#lem: šuba[multicoloured]; Irigal[1]TN; An[1]DN
#etcsl: line-id=55

56. |DU.DU|-e ba-ab-du₇-u₃
#tr.en: You are worthy of …….
#lem: X; du[perfect]
#etcsl: line-id=56

57. barag mah-ha saŋ il₂-la-a ba-ab-du₇-me-en₃
#tr.en: You are one who is entitled to hold high his head on the lofty dais.
#lem: barag[sanctum]; mah[great]; saŋ[head]; il[raise]; du[perfect]
#etcsl: line-id=57

58. {ŋiš}gu-za za-gin₃-na dur₂ ŋar-ra-a ba-ab-du₇-u₃
#tr.en: You are one who is worthy of sitting on the shining throne.
#lem: guza[chair]; zagin[lapis lazuli]; dur[buttocks]; ŋar[put]; du[perfect]
#etcsl: line-id=58

59. saŋ-zu men gun₃-a ba-ab-du₇-u₃
#tr.en: Your head is worthy of the brilliant crown.
#lem: saŋ[head]; men[tiara]; gunu[speckled]; du[perfect]
#etcsl: line-id=59

60. bar-zu-še₃ {tug₂}zulumhi sud-de₃ ba-ab-du₇-u₃
#tr.en: Your body is worthy of the long fleecy garment.
#lem: bar[outside]; zulumhi[fleece]; sud[distant]; du[perfect]
#etcsl: line-id=60

61. tug₂ nam-lugal-la₂-ka šag₄ la₂-a ba-ab-du₇-u₃
#tr.en: You are worthy of being dressed in the royal garb.
#lem: tug[textile]; namlugal[kingship]; šag[heart]; la[hang]; du[perfect]
#etcsl: line-id=61

62. mitum-ma a₂ il₂-de₃ ba-ab-du₇-u₃
#tr.en: You are suited to hold the @fsux{mitum} weapon in your arm.
#lem: mitum[divine weapon]; a[arm]; il[raise]; du[perfect]
#etcsl: line-id=62

63. {ŋiš}tukul-a dub₃ bad-ba₉-re₆ ba-ab-du₇-u₃
#tr.en: You are suited to run fast with the battle-mace.
#lem: tukul[weapon]; dub[knee]; bad[open]; du[perfect]
#etcsl: line-id=63

64. ti sud {ŋiš}pan si sa₂-e-de₃ ba-ab-du₇-u₃
#tr.en: You are suited to hit accurately with the barbed arrows and the bow.
#lem: ti[arrow]; sud[distant]; pana[bow]; si[horn]; sa[equal]; du[perfect]
#etcsl: line-id=64

65. {ŋiš}ilar {kuš}gur₂₁!(TUM){ur₃}-ra zag keše₂-ra₂-a ba-ab-du₇-u₃
#tr.en: You are suited to fasten the throw-stick and the sling to your side.
#lem: illar[weapon: bow? throwstick? javelin?]; guru[shield]; zag[side]; kešed[bind]; du[perfect]
#etcsl: line-id=65

66. šu-zu-še₃ ŋidru kug-ge ba-ab-du₇-u₃
#tr.en: Your hand is worthy of the holy sceptre.
#lem: šu[hand]; ŋidru[scepter]; kug[pure]; du[perfect]
#etcsl: line-id=66

67. ŋiri₃-zu-še₃ {kuš}e-sir₂ kug-ge ba-ab-du₇-u₃
#tr.en: Your feet are worthy of the holy shoes.
#lem: ŋiri[foot]; esir[sandal(s)]; kug[pure]; du[perfect]
#etcsl: line-id=67

68. dub₃-tuku-me-en₃ har-ra-an-na kaš₄ di-de₃ ba-ab-du₇-u₃
#tr.en: You are a fast runner suited to race on the road.
#lem: dubtuku[runner]; harran[route]; kaš[run]; di[speak]; du[perfect]
#etcsl: line-id=68

69. amar za-gin₃-na-gin₇ gaba kug-ŋa₂ a-ne di-de₃ ba-ab-du₇-u₃
#tr.en: You are worthy to delight yourself on my holy breast like a pure calf.
#lem: amar[calf]; zagin[lapis lazuli]; gaba[breast]; kug[pure]; ene[pleasure?]; di[speak]; du[perfect]
#etcsl: line-id=69

70. šag₄ ki aŋ₂-zu-u₃ ud he₂-em-su₃-re₆-e
#tr.en: May your love be lasting!
#lem: šag[heart]; ki[place]; aŋ[measure]; ud[sun]; sud[distant]
#etcsl: line-id=70

71. an-ne₂ mi-ri-in-ak na-da-ab-kur₂-re
#tr.en: @wDN{An} has determined this for you, and may he never alter it!
#lem: An[1]DN; ak[do]; kur[different]
#etcsl: line-id=71

72. {d}en-lil₂ lu₂ nam tar-tar-re-de₃ šu na-an-ni-ib-bal-e
#tr.en: May @wDN{Enlil}, the decreer of fates, never change it!”}
#lem: Enlil[1]DN; lu[person]; nam[fate]; tar[cut]; šu[hand]; bala[turn]
#etcsl: line-id=72

73. {d}inana-ke₄ mi₂ mu-ni-in-dug₄
#tr.en: Thus @wDN{Inana} treated him tenderly.
#lem: Inanak[1]DN; mi[cvne]; dug[speak]
#etcsl: line-id=73

